text: >-
  9/10/2025 12:23:34 PM

  BLAKEBEDNARZ

  O•C

  @ Measure

  Wick noints on the man

  1: 4,637 t | Mediar 4,699 . 11

  The person is observed at 12:23:34 already running and covers 220 feet in the
  next 15 seconds.

  That means their average speed during those 15 seconds is:

  220 ft ÷ 15 s = 14.666... ft/s (exactly 44/3 ft/s).

  We need to find when they crossed the start line, which was 80 feet before the
  position where we saw them at

  12:23:34.

  So the question is really: how many seconds before 12:23:34 did they cross the
  start line, assuming they ran at the

  same constant speed the whole time?

  Distance to cover to reach the observation point from the start line = 80 ft

  Speed = 220 ft / 15 s = 14.666... ft/s

  Time to cover those 80 ft = 80 ft ÷ (220 ft / 15 s) = 80 × (15 / 220) = (80 ×
  15) / 220 = 1200 / 220 = 120 / 22 = 60 /

  11 seconds

  60 ÷ 11 = 5.454545... seconds

  So they crossed the start line 60/11 seconds (about 5.45 seconds) before
  12:23:34.

  Now subtract that from 12:23:34:

  12:23:34 minus 5 full seconds = 12:23:29

  Then subtract the remaining 0.454545... seconds (which is exactly 5/11 of a
  second).

  So the exact start time is:

  12:23:34 - 60/11 seconds = 12:23:28 + (11/11 - 5/11) seconds = 12:23:28 and
  6/11 of a second.

  Or more cleanly:

  12:23:34 - 5 and 5/11 seconds = 12:23:28 and (1 - 5/11) = 12:23:28 and 6/11
  seconds.

  Therefore, they began running (crossed the start line) at exactly:

  12:23:28 + 6/11 seconds (approximately 12:23:28.545).

  If you want it in pure seconds notation: 12:23:28.54545... (repeating 45).

  Charlie Kirk was fatally shot at 12:23:30 p.m. MDT on September 10, 2025,
  during a speaking event at Utah Valley

  University in Orem, Utah. This precise timestamp comes from official
  investigations, eyewitness accounts, and

  video analyses reviewed by multiple outlets, including a Deseret News reporter
  who described seeing blood from

  Kirk's neck wound immediately after the shot rang out. Police dispatch
  recordings confirm the initial report of

  "shots fired" and Kirk down at exactly 12:23 p.m., with forensic video
  synchronization pinpointing the 30-second

  mark as the bullet impact.
